Text: "Abstract algebra studies operations through the identities they satisfy,
       deliberately ignoring the internal nature of the elements. The chapter
       moves from a single closed operation to monoids and groups, then studies
       structure-preserving maps, rings, and fields. It concludes with quotient
       objects and group actions, two constructions that reveal how algebraic
       structures decompose and how they act as symmetries of other objects.

       Three questions organize the discussion: what data constitute the
       structure, which equations are required, and which maps preserve those
       equations? Keeping these questions separate prevents notation from
       concealing the distinction between a carrier set, its operations, and
       the properties imposed on them."
Id: "b9195008-47f2-4dae-be3e-0886194e6bd0"
